    "https://careers.nmsu.edu/jobs/financial-aid-specialist-las-cruces-new-mexico-united-states-2272f46f-fdaa-45cf-922c-2d8534d64e34": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "Financial Aid Specialist - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Why NMSU? Aggie Perks Compensation and Benefits Applicant Resources View Jobs Applicant Login Kiosk mode Financial Aid Specialist 504030 Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Staff Staff Full-time Closing at: Oct 4 2026 - 23:55 MDT Add to favorites View favorites Department Contact: Maria Hernandez, 575-646-7598, mgh1@nmsu.edu Internal or External Search: External - Open to all applicants Advertising Summary: The University Financial Aid and Scholarship Services Department is seeking a dependable, highly motivated student centered individual with excellent customer services skills to join the Financial Aid Team. Position Details Position Title: Financial Aid Specialist College/Division: Student Enrollment and Success Department: 521040-UNIV FIN AID & SCHOLARSHIP SVCS Location: Las Cruces Offsite Location (if applicable): Target Hourly/Salary Rate: $16.83 Appointment Full-time Equivalency: 1.0 FLSA Status : Non-Exempt Bargaining Unit Announcement: This is a bargaining unit position with American Federation of State, County & Municipal Employees (AFSCME). Contingent Upon Funding: Not Applicable Standard Work Schedule: Standard (M-F, 8-5) If Not a Standard Work Schedule: Job Duties and Responsibilities: The Financial Aid Specialist serves as a primary point of contact for prospective and current students, families, faculty, staff, and the public regarding financial aid and scholarship programs. This position provides exceptional customer service through in-person interactions, Teams communications, and email correspondence while assisting students throughout the financial aid process. The incumbent reviews, verifies, and processes financial aid documentation, ensures compliance with federal, state, and institutional regulations, and maintains the accuracy and integrity of student financial aid records. Customer Service and Student Support Provide outstanding customer service to prospective and current students, parents, faculty, staff, and community members through multiple service channels including front counter, Teams, and email. Answer inquiries regarding financial aid and scholarships. Counsel and advise students and families regarding financial aid programs, eligibility requirements, application procedures, award status, and required documentation. Research, investigate, and resolve student questions, concerns, and complex issues related to financial aid transactions and processes. Refer students to appropriate university departments or offices when specialized assistance is needed. Maintain a comprehensive knowledge of university programs, policies, procedures, resources, and student services. Compliance and Regulatory Responsibilities Apply federal, state, and institutional financial aid policies, regulations, and procedures consistently and accurately. Maintain compliance with highly regulated financial aid programs and reporting requirements. Review student records to ensure proper application of laws, regulations, and eligibility requirements. Assist in identifying and correcting discrepancies within student records. Protect the confidentiality and integrity of student information in accordance with FERPA and other applicable regulations. Communication, Training, and Reporting Communicate application status updates and eligibility determinations to students and families. Participate in outreach activities, workshops, information sessions, and recruitment events as assigned. Collaboration and Professional Development Collaborate with university departments, home offices, and campus partners to ensure effective student service delivery. Participate in committees, conferences, meetings, and professional development activities. Maintain current knowledge of federal, state, and institutional financial aid regulations and best practices. Perform other duties as assigned in support of departmental and university goals. Position Working Conditions Frequent interaction with students, parents, faculty, staff, and external stakeholders. High-volume customer service environment requiring multitasking and attention to detail. Regular use of computer systems, student information systems, and office equipment. Qualifications Required Education and Experience: High School diploma or higher degree. Equivalent Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: Special Certification/Licensure: Working Conditions and Physical Effort Environment: Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment. Physical Effort: No or very limited physical effort required. Lifting Requirements: Requires handling of average-weight objects up to 10 pounds or some standing or walking. Risk: No or very limited exposure to physical risk. Recruitment Summary We are New Mexico’s land-grant institution and a comprehensive research university dedicated to teaching, research public service and outreach at all levels. NMSU is a welcoming community of talented faculty, staff and students who are working together to make a difference. We are a NASA Space Grant College, a Hispanic-serving institution (HSI), a minority-serving institution (MSI) and home to the first Honors College in New Mexico. We offer an accessible education that shapes bright futures. NMSU provides learning opportunities to a diverse population of students and community members at four campuses, Cooperative Extension offices located in each of New Mexico’s 33 counties, 12 research and science centers, and through distance education. NMS U Global Campus Since 1888, NMSU has proudly embodied this tradition, building relationships that last a lifetime while serving students who want to earn their degree and grow in their field. Today, NMSU Global Campus provides flexible, career-focused online education that helps our students transform their lives – and the lives of the people they love – through over 70 degree and certificate programs, skill-building microlearning courses, and career and talent development. NMSU Main Campus Located in Las Cruces, NM, New Mexico State University's 900-acre main campus is located at the crossroads of I-10 and I-25 in the Southwestern United States. As a thriving center of higher education, deeply rooted in the regional tradition, its role as a comprehensive university is recognized throughout the state. Doña Ana Community College Founded in 1973 in collaboration with local school districts to support occupational education, DACC is now a leading community college that provides transformative educational opportunities that meet the workforce needs of Doña Ana County. With a focus on access, innovation and excellence, DACC offers over ninety degrees and certificates, adult education, specialized workforce training, and small business assistance. Alamogordo Campus Established in 1958 to serve the needs of the airmen and families stationed at Holloman Air Force Base located only 10 miles west of Alamogordo, NMSUA is a community college with a long history of excellence that is supported by a caring community of hard-working students and dedicated faculty and staff. The campus is situated “on the hill” above Alamogordo and provides inspiring views of the city and the Tularosa Basin, offering the perfect venue for creative and motivated learning. Grants Campus NMSU Grants was established as a branch of New Mexico State University in 1968 through the cooperative efforts of New Mexico State University and Grants Municipal Schools. As a two-year branch community college, NMSU Grants serves the local communities in Cibola and McKinley counties, including the Pueblos of Acoma, Laguna, and Zuni, as well as Tohajiilee, San Mateo, San Rafael, Cubero, the City of Grants, and the Village of Milan. Special Instructions to Applicants The electronic application is the *official* document that will be used to qualify applicants. Paper/email documents will not be accepted. Required documents must be attached to this application. EEO Statement New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Requesting an Accommodation Individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and New Mexico State University policy, if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply, interview, or complete onboarding for a position with New Mexico State University, or if you cannot use the online application system, please visit our Accessibility & Accommodations page to initiate an accommodation request Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 885a9389 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 521040-UNIV FIN AID & SCHOLARSHIP SVCS 521040-UNIV FIN AID & SCHOLARSHIP SVCS Locations Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States First Name (required) fe6b8730 Last Name (required) 2ca56072 Email (required) 01417c43 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Executive Assistant 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Doña Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 940600-DACC ACADEMIC SUPP DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Administrative Assistant Intermediate Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 500764-FS PROJECT DESIGN Join our team! Provide administrative support through communication, scheduling, requisitions, data management, reporting, and reconciliations. Coordinate meetings and events while serving as a liaison and supporting daily operations. Extension Specialist/ 4-H STEM Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 314000-4 H AND YOUTH DEVELOPMENT PGM UNIT The Cooperative Extension Service at NMSU is actively recruiting for a 4H STEM Specialist. This is a tenure-track, 12-month appointment.  Apply today! Student Program Coordinator Senior Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 380001-GRADUATE SCHOOL The Graduate School is seeking a detail-oriented and organized Student Program Coordinator, Sr. to support graduate students throughout their academic journey, from admission through graduation. This position processes and maintains student records and documentation related to admissions, academic milestones, program requirements, final examinations, thesis and dissertation submission, and degree certification. The successful candidate will work closely with students, faculty, and academic departments to interpret requirements, resolve record and processing issues, and ensure accurate and timely completion of Graduate School processes. Strong organizational skills, attention to detail, sound judgment, and a commitment to excellent customer service are essential for success in this role. Extension Specialist/Agronomist/ Soil Fertility 1780 East University Avenue, NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States, 88003 311200-EXTENSN PLANT SCIENCES Inviting applications for an Extension Agronomy/Soil Fertility Specialist, Assistant Professor (tenure-track, 12-month) position located at the Ag Science Center in Artesia, NM. CES County Program Assistant Remote Locations, New Mexico, United States 310600-ADMIN PRGM GUADALUPE CTY If you are interested in 4H, we have a job for you.  We are searching for a Program Assistant to work with the Cooperative Extension Agent to deliver programming and services to 4-H youth and other constituents.\n\n** This position is located in Guadalupe County, Santa Rosa, NM.** Apply Now First Name (required) dcdc9ffc Last Name (required) f6570da8 Email (required) c38bcb4c Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Diversity & Inclusion New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Quick Links About NMSU Contact Us Privacy Policy Search NMSU Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by New Mexico State University - Board of Regents . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
