    "https://careers.nmsu.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-ornamental-landscape-horticulture-las-cruces-new-mexico-united-states": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "Assistant Professor/Ornamental & Landscape Horticulture - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Why NMSU? Aggie Perks Compensation and Benefits Applicant Resources View Jobs Applicant Login Kiosk mode Assistant Professor/Ornamental & Landscape Horticulture 504029 Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Faculty 9-Month Faculty Full-Time Closing at: Oct 1 2026 - 23:55 MDT Add to favorites View favorites Department Contact: Dennis Lozada, 575-646-5171, dlozada@nmsu.edu Internal or External Search: External - Open to all applicants Advertising Summary: The Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences (PES) at New Mexico State University (NMSU) is searching for a new faculty member in Horticulture with an emphasis on Ornamental and Landscape Horticulture. Position Details Position Title: Assistant Professor/Ornamental & Landscape Horticulture College/Division: Agricultural,Consumer & Env Sci Col Department: 301400-PLANT AND ENVIRONMENTAL SCIENCES Location: Las Cruces Offsite Location (if applicable): Target Hourly/Salary Rate: Commensurate with qualifications Appointment Full-time Equivalency: 1.0 FLSA Status : Exempt Bargaining Unit Announcement: This is a bargaining unit position with the National Education Association (NEA). Contingent Upon Funding: Not Applicable Standard Work Schedule: Standard (M-F, 8-5) If Not a Standard Work Schedule: Job Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences (PES) at New Mexico State University (NMSU) is searching for a new faculty member in Horticulture. The 9-month tenure-track position is 75% teaching and 25% research and outreach. PES is specifically seeking candidates who are interested in building upon our long-term commitment to Urban Horticulture, with emphasis on Ornamental and Landscape Horticulture. The new faculty member will teach undergraduate and graduate courses required for horticulture, agronomy, and other majors in the Department, potentially including Introduction to Plant Science, Hydroponics, Landscape Design, Ornamental Plants, Care and Selection of Houseplants, and Seminar. Development of new courses in the candidate's area of expertise at the urban-agricultural interface, such as resilient landscape design, urban improvement (urban forests, urban ecology, biodiversity, horticulture in the built environment, herbaceous and non-herbaceous plant selection, etc.) and regenerative agriculture is encouraged. The incumbent will mentor undergraduate and graduate students, provide leadership in PES horticulture research and teaching programs, assist students in job placements and internships, and co-advise the NMSU Horticulture Forum. Service to the profession and to university, college, and departmental committees is expected. Outreach with stakeholders (e.g., Master Gardeners, New Mexico State Forestry Division, New Mexico Grown Coalition, Municipalities and Urban Planners) is also expected. The faculty member will have opportunities to work across departments and colleges, including the off-campus Agricultural Science Centers, with specialists in horticulture, soils, agribusiness, agricultural and extension education, crop breeding, economics, plant genetics, plant physiology, molecular biology, human nutrition, renewable energy, economics, and social sciences. Research areas may include sustainable landscaping and permaculture, urban food systems, climate resilient landscape design, urban ecology and biodiversity, green infrastructure and nature-based solutions or human health and social sustainability. There is also potential for research collaboration with community colleges and other universities that offer specialized urban horticulture programs focusing on sustainable plant production, green infrastructure, and landscape management in urban and developed environments. The State of New Mexico and NMSU provide unique and diverse opportunities for teaching, research, and outreach related to urban horticulture. NMSU's Horticulture program offers training in Hydroponics, Greenhouse and Nursery Management, Turfgrass Management, and Ornamentals, directly applying to urban landscapes. Las Cruces, New Mexico's second largest city and one of the fastest-growing urban areas in the state, currently faces classic urban horticulture challenges such as climate adapted plant material, poor soils, heat islands, water scarcity and irrigation efficiency and demand for urban green spaces in the built environment. There is an active Extension/outreach Urban Horticulture program that provides robust support for urban residents. The faculty position is well-aligned to NMSU's mission as a land-grant institution, to address urgent climate and water challenges, support community needs, strengthen high-impact teaching in degree programs in horticulture and the Department's existing outreach, research, and teaching capacity. The candidate will also be expected to foster collaborations and participate in activities and on research teams that support the work of the Center for Excellence in Sustainable Food and Agricultural Systems (CESFAS). New Mexico State University is the state's land-grant institution, with more than 22,000 undergraduate and graduate students on the main campus in Las Cruces and four satellite campuses. The Plant and Environmental Sciences (PES) Department is part of the College of Agricultural, Consumer and Environmental Sciences, which is home to seven other academic departments, five extension departments, and approximately 150 faculty members and 1,800 students. PES consists of approximately 46 faculty and research scientists, and 160 undergraduate and 60 graduate students (MS and PhD). Teaching and research concentrations in PES include horticulture, agronomy, plant breeding and genetic improvement, molecular biology, plant physiology, ecology, and environmental, water, and soil sciences. An active mentoring program is in place for new faculty to onboard with senior faculty and successfully progress through the faculty ranks. Research opportunities exist across NMSU's network of 12 Agricultural Science Centers located around the state, including several facilities near the NMSU main campus. A new container farm laboratory is housed on the NMSU-Grants campus and serves as a prototype for economic growth and a means to combat climate change, food insecurity, and inequities in STEM education. Core facilities for microscopy, tissue culture, advanced chemical and omics analysis, and molecular biology are available to complement laboratory, greenhouse, and field experimental facilities. Opportunities exist to participate in undergraduate and graduate training programs sponsored by USDA, NIH, NSF, and HSI/MSI programs. Additionally, NMSU actively participates with numerous state, tribal and federal agencies. For more information on PES, see https://pes.nmsu.edu. The Plant and Environmental Sciences (PES) Department is part of the College of Agricultural, Consumer and Environmental Sciences, which is home to seven other academic departments, five extension departments, and approximately 150 faculty members and 1,800 students. PES consists of approximately 46 faculty and research scientists, and 160 undergraduate and 60 graduate students (MS and PhD). Teaching and research concentrations in PES include horticulture, agronomy, plant breeding and genetic improvement, molecular biology, plant physiology, ecology, and environmental, water, and soil sciences. An active mentoring program is in place for new faculty to onboard with senior faculty and successfully progress through the faculty ranks. *** Application materials must include: (a) curriculum vitae; (b) statement of teaching philosophy and experience (2-page maximum); (c) statement of research interests (2-page maximum); (d) contact information for three references, and (e) undergraduate and graduate transcripts. Qualifications Required Education and Experience: Ph.D. (awarded by hire date) in Horticulture/Plant Science, Landscape Architecture, Agricultural Sustainability/Sustainable Design, Regenerative Landscaping, or a closely related field. The successful candidate will show a commitment to excellence and specific evidence of: (1) teaching and research experience in urban horticulture, regenerative agriculture, landscape design, or urban improvement; (2) demonstrated ability to communicate with diverse audiences including students, academic, industry, and stakeholders; (3) demonstrated ability to publish research in leading research and academic outlets with potential to compete successfully for external research funding; and (4) an ability to contribute to undergraduate and graduate education and mentor diverse undergraduate and graduate students. The department's student population is diverse and multicultural, and the ability to enjoy and thrive in this collaborative environment will be necessary. Equivalent Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: Background in experimental design and analysis; postdoctoral work with attraction of extramural support; demonstrated evidence of engaging students, community members, and scientists on issues relating to horticulture; ability to conduct research in urban horticulture and sustainable landscapes; ability to teach undergraduate and graduate courses required for horticulture, agronomy and other majors including ornamental plant identification and landscape design; research and teaching experience in landscape design, landscape resilience and/or productive landscapes and food systems; demonstrated evidence of engaging and mentoring students; ability to develop a nationally recognized program in resilient landscape design, regenerative agriculture, and/or urban agriculture. Special Certification/Licensure: Working Conditions and Physical Effort Environment: Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment. Physical Effort: No or very limited physical effort required. Lifting Requirements: Requires handling of average-weight objects up to 10 pounds or some standing or walking. Risk: No or very limited exposure to physical risk. Recruitment Summary We are New Mexico’s land-grant institution and a comprehensive research university dedicated to teaching, research public service and outreach at all levels. NMSU is a welcoming community of talented faculty, staff and students who are working together to make a difference. We are a NASA Space Grant College, a Hispanic-serving institution (HSI), a minority-serving institution (MSI) and home to the first Honors College in New Mexico. We offer an accessible education that shapes bright futures. NMSU provides learning opportunities to a diverse population of students and community members at four campuses, Cooperative Extension offices located in each of New Mexico’s 33 counties, 12 research and science centers, and through distance education. NMS U Global Campus Since 1888, NMSU has proudly embodied this tradition, building relationships that last a lifetime while serving students who want to earn their degree and grow in their field. Today, NMSU Global Campus provides flexible, career-focused online education that helps our students transform their lives – and the lives of the people they love – through over 70 degree and certificate programs, skill-building microlearning courses, and career and talent development. NMSU Main Campus Located in Las Cruces, NM, New Mexico State University's 900-acre main campus is located at the crossroads of I-10 and I-25 in the Southwestern United States. As a thriving center of higher education, deeply rooted in the regional tradition, its role as a comprehensive university is recognized throughout the state. Doña Ana Community College Founded in 1973 in collaboration with local school districts to support occupational education, DACC is now a leading community college that provides transformative educational opportunities that meet the workforce needs of Doña Ana County. With a focus on access, innovation and excellence, DACC offers over ninety degrees and certificates, adult education, specialized workforce training, and small business assistance. Alamogordo Campus Established in 1958 to serve the needs of the airmen and families stationed at Holloman Air Force Base located only 10 miles west of Alamogordo, NMSUA is a community college with a long history of excellence that is supported by a caring community of hard-working students and dedicated faculty and staff. The campus is situated “on the hill” above Alamogordo and provides inspiring views of the city and the Tularosa Basin, offering the perfect venue for creative and motivated learning. Grants Campus NMSU Grants was established as a branch of New Mexico State University in 1968 through the cooperative efforts of New Mexico State University and Grants Municipal Schools. As a two-year branch community college, NMSU Grants serves the local communities in Cibola and McKinley counties, including the Pueblos of Acoma, Laguna, and Zuni, as well as Tohajiilee, San Mateo, San Rafael, Cubero, the City of Grants, and the Village of Milan. Special Instructions to Applicants The electronic application is the *official* document that will be used to qualify applicants. Paper/email documents will not be accepted. Required documents must be attached to this application. EEO Statement New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Requesting an Accommodation Individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and New Mexico State University policy, if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply, interview, or complete onboarding for a position with New Mexico State University, or if you cannot use the online application system, please visit our Accessibility & Accommodations page to initiate an accommodation request Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 3c1bfe76 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 301400-PLANT AND ENVIRONMENTAL SCIENCES 301400-PLANT AND ENVIRONMENTAL SCIENCES Locations Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States First Name (required) 8f92cd91 Last Name (required) 2e967e18 Email (required) e2fbee5a Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Executive Assistant 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Doña Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 940600-DACC ACADEMIC SUPP DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Administrative Assistant Intermediate Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 500764-FS PROJECT DESIGN Join our team! Provide administrative support through communication, scheduling, requisitions, data management, reporting, and reconciliations. Coordinate meetings and events while serving as a liaison and supporting daily operations. Extension Specialist/ 4-H STEM Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 314000-4 H AND YOUTH DEVELOPMENT PGM UNIT The Cooperative Extension Service at NMSU is actively recruiting for a 4H STEM Specialist. This is a tenure-track, 12-month appointment.  Apply today! Student Program Coordinator Senior Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 380001-GRADUATE SCHOOL The Graduate School is seeking a detail-oriented and organized Student Program Coordinator, Sr. to support graduate students throughout their academic journey, from admission through graduation. This position processes and maintains student records and documentation related to admissions, academic milestones, program requirements, final examinations, thesis and dissertation submission, and degree certification. The successful candidate will work closely with students, faculty, and academic departments to interpret requirements, resolve record and processing issues, and ensure accurate and timely completion of Graduate School processes. Strong organizational skills, attention to detail, sound judgment, and a commitment to excellent customer service are essential for success in this role. Extension Specialist/Agronomist/ Soil Fertility 1780 East University Avenue, NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States, 88003 311200-EXTENSN PLANT SCIENCES Inviting applications for an Extension Agronomy/Soil Fertility Specialist, Assistant Professor (tenure-track, 12-month) position located at the Ag Science Center in Artesia, NM. CES County Program Assistant Remote Locations, New Mexico, United States 310600-ADMIN PRGM GUADALUPE CTY If you are interested in 4H, we have a job for you.  We are searching for a Program Assistant to work with the Cooperative Extension Agent to deliver programming and services to 4-H youth and other constituents.\n\n** This position is located in Guadalupe County, Santa Rosa, NM.** Apply Now First Name (required) 7e898ed8 Last Name (required) 5c7390b8 Email (required) 45a9db21 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Diversity & Inclusion New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Quick Links About NMSU Contact Us Privacy Policy Search NMSU Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by New Mexico State University - Board of Regents . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
